+# Dual-review R2 — p0-mcp-stdio-l2-r2 (Pi REJECT fixes)
+
+## Method
+
+I did not rely on the patch file alone. I:
+- Read the working-tree code at the exact hunks (message-router.ts:1827-1923, 3495-3616; server.ts:6480-6496, 7025-7086, 7108-7110).
+- Rebuilt the test dist (`tsc -p tsconfig.test.json`, clean build) and ran `node --test .test-dist/tests/mcp-stdio-l2-gate.test.js` myself → **7/7 pass**.
+- Empirically probed an edge case the suite doesn't cover (`patch.env: null`).
+- Traced the extension round-trip end-to-end (McpServerForm.tsx buildConfig sends literal `***`; server restores).
+- Checked every `listServers()`/meta broadcast path for raw-secret leakage.
+- Scanned out-of-scope batches (SEC-A/D/E, VOICE, MCPO-01 `require_grant` flip) for MCP regressions.
+
+## Pi blocker #1 — `mcp.update {enabled:true}` on disabled stdio: CLOSED ✓
+
+`mcpStdioSpawnSurfaceChanged` (message-router.ts:3542-3545) now treats `enabled false→true` as a spawn-surface change. The gate runs pre-write, fail-closed without `requestConfirmation` (message-router.ts:1877-1881). Test `"mcp.update enabled-only on disabled stdio requires L2"` passes and I confirmed the error leaves `config.mcp.servers.disabledstdio.enabled === false` untouched. `toggle_server` re-enable path also gates (message-router.ts:1908-1921). I verified no `enabled:true` transition can reach `replaceMcpServers` un-gated on either path (http→stdio, stdio→stdio, disabled→enabled all covered; stdio→http and enable→disable correctly skip since no spawn).
+
+## Pi blocker #2 — `***` corrupts persisted secrets: CLOSED ✓
+
+`mergeMcpServerPreservingSecrets`/`restoreMaskedRecord` (message-router.ts:3565-3595): `***` echoes restore the prior disk value; `***` with no existing key is dropped — the mask literal can never be persisted. I verified the real UI flow: redacted metas → form prefill with `***` → `buildConfig` re-sends `***` → server restores (test `"mcp.update preserves secrets when client sends ***"` passes; `API_KEY: "real-secret-value"` + `trust_level: "trusted"` both land on disk). New-value replacement, key deletion via empty-object patch, and env-change re-confirm all behave correctly. Both redaction producers (`redactMcpServersForBroadcast`, pre-existing `redactConfigForBroadcast`) use the same `***` token — consistent.
+
+## ADR-020 checklist
+
+- **Declaration**: present (r1, unchanged); Surface n/a (trust root), Compose mcp-server, Autonomy single, Trust L2 force-high fail-closed, Channel community. No "中层 Agent" framing. ✓
+- **originWs**: `requestConfirmation` wired with `{ originWs: ws }` (server.ts:7046-7047) — P1-2 satisfied. ✓
+- **Trust monotonicity**: add/update/toggle_server all force-high, `autoConfirmEligible: false`, fail closed without channel. ✓
+- **Broadcast redaction**: all 9 paths redacted (list, toggle_enabled, add, update, delete, toggle_server responses + servers_updated/status_changed/tools_changed emitters); remaining `listServers()` uses (message-router.ts:2828, server.ts:5317) never reach the wire. ✓
+- **Out-of-scope batches**: `require_grant` default true (config.ts:335) is stricter; no production call site passes `requireGrant: false` (companion-http.ts:466, 506 pass only `bodyCallerId`). SEC-A/D/E/VOICE don't touch MCP. ✓
+
+## Nits (non-blocking)
+
+1. **message-router.ts:3571 (reachable via 3589/3592)** — `mcp.update` with `patch: { env: null }` (or `headers: null`) throws `TypeError: Cannot convert undefined or null to object` from `Object.entries(null)`. `validateMcpServerConfig` doesn't catch `null` (it satisfies `typeof null === "object"`), and the throw happens pre-validation. Fail-closed — caught by the ws handler (server.ts:7082-7086), no config write, no spawn — but the client gets an internal-error string instead of a clean validation message. Guard `incoming != null` or validate patch types.
+2. **Test gaps carried from r1** — `mcp.update` command/args/cwd re-confirm, `toggle_server` deny path, and `status_changed` redaction still untested (the two Pi-fix tests + add-gate/http/redact tests are solid).
+3. **Stale comment** — mcp/types.ts:109-110 claims env/headers "are NOT a concern here" on the wire; now contradicted by the redaction this batch adds.
+4. **`mcp.toggle_enabled` global resume** (message-router.ts:1829-1834) spawns all per-server-enabled stdio servers with no L2 when the master switch flips on. Trust envelope is intact (every spawn definition was L2-approved at add/update; identical to startup spawn), so this is not a bypass of the Pi blockers — but it is philosophically inconsistent with the new per-server re-enable gates; a comment or defense-in-depth gate would close the asymmetry.
+
+Both Pi blockers are fully closed, verified in real code and by running the suite myself. No blocking issues found.
+
+VERDICT: APPROVE_WITH_NITS
